      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9646780::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC9646780::web::002::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relevant SRO in FeNiCrMn particularly involves Mn/Cr clustering.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chemical short-range order alters dislocation kinetics in concentrated FCC solid solutions.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9646780::web::002::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "SRO locally increases lattice friction in FeNiCrMn.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9646780::web::002::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At intermediate temperatures and strain rates, SRO domains intermittently pin dislocations in FeNiCrMn.",
      "field": "hypothesis/mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Intermittent dislocation pinning by SRO produces dynamic strain aging.",
      "field": "hypothesis/mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increasing SRO can strengthen an FCC concentrated solid solution and modify its strain-hardening capacity.",
      "field": "mechanism/predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9646780::web::002::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "SRO-promoted FeNiCrMn will have greater yield strength than minimally ordered quenched FeNiCrMn at intermediate temperatures and strain rates.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9646780::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC9646780::web::002::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "SRO-promoted FeNiCrMn will show non-monotonic strain hardening and serrated flow relative to the quenched baseline.",
      "field": "hypothesis/predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The extent of mechanically generated SRO can depend on strain rate.",
      "field": "conditions/mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9646780::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At high temperatures, rapid diffusion homogenizes SRO and reduces the mechanical differences between annealed and quenched FeNiCrMn.",
      "field": "mechanism/predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At very low temperatures, insufficient diffusion prevents thermally mediated SRO development.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9646780::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC9646780::web::002::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed mechanism is limited to a diffusion window that permits short-range ordering but avoids long-range ordering or phase separation.",
